  "full_response": "Native Americans are the indigenous peoples of the United States, with rich histories, cultures, and contributions that are integral to the national fabric. There are numerous tribes, each with distinct languages, traditions, and practices. Some of the well-known tribes include the Navajo, Cherokee, Sioux, Iroquois, and many others.\n\nUnderstanding Native American history involves recognizing their resilience and struggles. European colonization had a profound impact, leading to displacement, loss of life due to disease, and various forms of marginalization. Despite these challenges, Native American communities have worked to preserve their cultures, languages, and traditions.\n\nToday, Native Americans continue to celebrate their heritage through various cultural expressions, including art, music, and dance. They also play a crucial role in advocating for sovereignty, rights, and recognition within the U.S. political and social arenas.\n\nIt's important to approach the subject with respect, recognizing both the historical injustices faced and the ongoing contributions Native Americans make to society. Engaging with resources from Native communities themselves can provide deeper insight and understanding.",
